Subject: Does `cfa(,orthogonal.y=FALSE)`equal to `f1~~f2` ?
Message-ID: <2weZoM4WPgc.jWlURmZkCAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/2weZoM4WPgc/m/jWlURmZkCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

corr_model<-'
f1=~q1+q2+q3
f2=~q4+q4+q6
f3=~q7+q8+q9
#explicity indicate correlation between factors,it's dull to input when you have more than 10 factors
f1~~f2
f1~~f3
f2~~F3
'
res1<-cfa(corr_model,df)

When factors correlated,we know factors are not orthogonal.
without_corr_model<-'
f1=~q1+q2+q3
f2=~q4+q4+q6
f3=~q7+q8+q9
'
res2<-cfa(without_corr_model,df,orthogonal.y=FALSE)

Does `res1` alway equal to `res2`?

